2,1,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
3,1,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
4,1,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Minako,,"We need a structured system now. Our informal arrangement is breaking down, and we should determine what a truly even split looks like to avoid anyone unfairly subsidizing others.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I agree that clarity is helpful, though I hope we don't let the ledger replace our friendship. A bit of structure might actually save us from these clipped replies.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Asuka,,"Financials are one thing, but the daily reliability is the real issue. I often find the car missing or dirty when I need it. We need standards for availability and state.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Shion,,Logic dictates that we cannot build a fair system on guesswork. We need the real figures first. I want an honest picture of the costs and who is actually driving.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I just think it's a lot of work to organize everything. Maybe we can find a way to make it less stressful for everyone to manage?,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, the stress comes from the current ambiguity. If we establish clear rules for payments and scheduling, the daily friction will disappear.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. However, let's be careful not to create a system so rigid that we spend more time auditing each other than actually driving.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, a ""rigid"" system is better than a chaotic one. If the car isn't where it's supposed to be on a Tuesday morning, the system has failed.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, you're talking about symptoms. The cause is a lack of accountability. If we track the hours and the money precisely, the behavior will follow the logic of the cost.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,I guess... but the untangling of who owes what always feels so tense. I'm worried we'll just spend more time arguing over the numbers.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Minako,,"That is why we must look at the data objectively. We need to see the tax, insurance, and actual usage patterns to define what ""fair"" means in our specific case.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,A fair point. I'm curious if other households have solved this without turning their living room into a courtroom. Perhaps there's a more elegant approach.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"I care less about ""elegance"" and more about the state of the car at handover. If we don't address the maintenance and cleanliness, the cost split is irrelevant.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, ""elegance"" is often a mask for imprecision. I'm interested in the fuel receipts and the diary. We need to see the disparity between contribution and consumption.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just want it to be simpler. I'll look into the time it takes to manage this... if that helps.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Minako,,Let's proceed with the investigation. I will focus on the fixed costs and the usage patterns to establish a baseline for an even split.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall look into the human element and the practicalities of tracking. I'd prefer a solution that minimizes the need for constant negotiation.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Asuka,,I will investigate the car's condition and the frequency of use. I want to know why the car is often unavailable or neglected during the week.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Shion,,I will secure the financial data. I want to see the fuel receipts and the actual hours recorded. Let's see who has been coasting on others' generosity.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,Okay... I'll look into the diary and the checking process. I want to see how much time we actually spend on the administration.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
