33,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The fixed costs are quite high, over 280,000 yen. Combined with the weekly scheduling conflicts, it's clear that a simple split isn't accounting for the actual utility of the car.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems that the ""administrative burden"" is a real risk. I've found that overly precise tracking can take significant time and, more importantly, create social friction.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The data confirms my frustration. The car is frequently returned empty and dirty, and the weekly recurring trips are the first to be disrupted. This is a failure of basic respect.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"As I suspected, the fuel contributions are a mess. Some of you are paying for others' commutes. The disparity is logically unacceptable; we cannot ignore the actual consumption figures.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I looked at the diary... and the checking period. It's not just the money. We spend so many hours just trying to figure out who owes what. It makes me feel... anxious.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, your anxiety is a result of the lack of a system. If we automate the split or set a flat fee based on the 280,000 yen baseline, the checking time vanishes.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, but a flat fee might just move the ""sore point"" to those who use it less. The real danger is the feeling of having to ""ask a favor"" for something we all own.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, you're obsessed with the fuel, but what about the state of the vehicle? If the car is unusable because it's filthy or out of gas, the ""fair"" payment is meaningless.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, cleanliness is a behavioral issue, but fuel is a financial one. I'm not interested in ""feelings"" of fairness; I'm interested in the actual numbers. The current gap is absurd.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,But when we checked the figures last time... everyone ended up feeling bad. The person checking felt like a villain. I don't want us to feel like that again.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We must balance precision with sustainability. If we track every single kilometer, we increase the friction @Daisuke fears. If we ignore it, we maintain the unfair subsidy.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Exactly. I've seen that the most successful arrangements avoid the ""auditor"" role entirely. We should avoid any system that requires us to police each other's every move.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,I don't care about policing; I care about reliability. I want a system where the car is guaranteed to be ready for the weekly recurring trips. That is a non-negotiable standard.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, avoiding the ""auditor"" role is just a way of allowing the free-riders to continue. If we don't have a precise mechanism for payment, the logical outcome is resentment.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,Is there a way to just... not have to talk about it every single night? The arranging and the untangling... it's just too much.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minako,,I believe we can find a middle ground. We can use the fixed costs as a base and implement a simplified usage fee that doesn't require daily auditing but reflects the reality.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I would support any option that prioritizes the harmony of the group over the absolute precision of the yen. Let's avoid the ""checking each other's figures"" trap.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I will support any option that includes a strict protocol for the car's state and a protected schedule for recurring trips. The ""experience"" of use must be standardized.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"I will only support an option that addresses the fuel disparity. A ""simplified"" fee is just another word for ""unfair"" if it doesn't reflect the actual hours of use.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I just want the one that is the easiest to manage. I can't handle the arguing over the receipts anymore.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
