60,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option A provides the most stability and eliminates the need for auditing, which addresses @Daisuke's anxiety and the fixed costs I found. It's a clean, fair split of time.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is the most elegant. It removes the need to ""ask for a favor"" or police each other's mileage. It preserves our social harmony by removing the transaction from the interaction.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is the only one that guarantees the car is where I expect it to be on a midweek morning. It protects the recurring trips by giving us dedicated ownership of the day.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A is logically flawed. It ignores the disparity in actual usage and fuel consumption. Someone who doesn't drive on their day still pays the same as someone who drives 200km.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Option A... sounds the quietest. No one has to untangle anything at the end of the week. We just know it's our day. I like that.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, while A isn't perfectly precise regarding fuel, it is the most sustainable. The cost of the ""administrative friction"" in Option B is higher than the cost of a slight fuel imbalance.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,I agree with @Minako. Option B is essentially a professional auditing firm in our living room. It's a recipe for the exact kind of resentment we're trying to avoid.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,Option B is a nightmare for reliability. A calendar is just a suggestion until someone fails to return the car on time. Option A creates a clear boundary of responsibility.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Minako, you're valuing ""quiet"" over ""correct."" Option B is the only one that ensures the person who uses the fuel pays for the fuel. That is the only logical way to handle a shared asset.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"Option B sounds like more of the same... more recording, more checking, more arguing. I don't think I can do that for another year.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minako,,Option C is too unbalanced; it places too much burden on one person and creates a power dynamic that doesn't fit our group. A and B are the only viable paths.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,Option C is essentially a landlord-tenant relationship. It would be a disaster for our friendship. Option A is the only choice that treats us as equals without making us accountants.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,Option C is out. It doesn't solve the state of the car issue; it just delegates it to one person who might be just as negligent. Option A ensures we are each responsible for our day.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"If we choose A, we are essentially agreeing to let the heavy users be subsidized by the light users. I find that logically offensive. Option B is the only fair solution.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I really don't like Option B. And Option C feels like we're just asking one person to do all the work. Option A feels... safe.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minako,,"We have a clear consensus on the emotional and practical costs. While @Shion prefers mathematical precision, the group's stability depends on reducing friction. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I concur. The goal is to stop the car from souring our relationships. Option A removes the catalyst for conflict. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Reliability and a guaranteed schedule are my priorities. Option A provides the only structural guarantee that the car will be available and that the user of the day is responsible for its state. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,"You are all choosing convenience over fairness. It is a disappointing lack of logical rigor, but I see the numbers are against me. I still believe B is the only honest choice.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'm voting for A. I just want us to be able to talk about other things besides the car.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
